body:
I've spent a couple days working on this issue with no result.
I tried to get a jsFiddle together but couldn't get dat.gui to integrate with it in order to demonstrate changing these values with no effect.

But the simple fact is:
With a WebGLRenderer and PerspectiveCamera, any attempt at altering sorting does nothing.
I even tried hacking three.js at one point to introduce a custom sort, but apparently, it's overridden or ignored.

The sample I used is as follows:

``` javascript
var gui = new dat.GUI();
var folder = gui.addFolder("renderDepth");

var R = new THREE.Mesh( new THREE.BoxGeometry(50, 50, 50), new THREE.MeshPhongMaterial({color:0xFF0000}) );
R.position.set(-10,-10,-10);
R.renderDepth = 3;
folder.add(R,"renderDepth").min(0).max(1000).step(1).name("Red").listen();
scene.add(R);

var G = new THREE.Mesh( new THREE.BoxGeometry(50, 50, 50), new THREE.MeshPhongMaterial({color:0x00FF00}) );
G.renderDepth = 2;
folder.add(G,"renderDepth").min(0).max(1000).step(1).name("Green").listen();
scene.add(G);

var B = new THREE.Mesh( new THREE.BoxGeometry(50, 50, 50), new THREE.MeshPhongMaterial({color:0x0000FF}) );
B.position.set(+10,+10,+10);
B.renderDepth = 1;
folder.add(B,"renderDepth").min(0).max(1000).step(1).name("Blue").listen();
scene.add(B);

folder.open();
```

I also noticed that very few pertinent questions on StackOverflow were answered and so I'm hoping this is enough of a bug to post this here.
